   "slug": "you-are-at-your-best-when-you-are-in-the-spirit",
   "order": 1,
   "title": "You Are at Your Best When You Are in the Spirit!",
   "summary": "The believer’s habitat is the Holy Spirit just as water is to fish, hole is to foxes and nest is to birds. Therefore, as a child of God, YOU ARE AT YOUR BEST WHEN YOU ARE IN THE SPIRIT.",
   "key_scripture": "Ephesians 5:18",
   "key_scripture_text": "And do not be drunk with wine, in which is dissipation; but be filled with the Spirit",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "The believer’s habitat is the Holy Spirit just as water is to fish, hole is to foxes and nest is to birds. Therefore, as a child of God, YOU ARE AT YOUR BEST WHEN YOU ARE IN THE SPIRIT. However, to be spirit full, you must be prayerful and addicted to fasting."
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "Prayer and fasting connects us to the Holy Spirit and the Holy Spirit release the power to perform - Philippians 1:19 For I know that this shall turn to my salvation through your prayer, and the supply of the Spirit of Jesus Christ,.’ When you are filled up with the Spirit, you are filled up with so much power and no man can withstand you – Isaiah 59:19 So shall they fear The name of the LORD from the west, And His glory from the rising of the sun; When the enemy comes in like a flood, The Spirit of the LORD will lift up a standard against him."
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "From today, get into prayer and fasting so as to access the fullness of His power. To be prayerless is to be powerless and fireless. Empty your stomach by waiting on God in fasting to fill tour spirit. Afflict your body to fatten your spirit man. As you sow to your spirit, you will reap power and glory."
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "As a serious Christian , let prayer and fasting be your obsession. YOU SHALL SEE THE GOODNESS OF THE LORD IN THE LAND OF THE LIVING IN JESUS NAME!"
    }
   ],
   "prayer": "O Lord, empower me to always seek Your face in Jesus Name!",
   "confession": "I am full of the Spirit!",
