   "title": "You Must Stretch Out to Spread Out — Part 2",
   "summary": "Don’t give up! You are advancing and exceling no matter what in Jesus Name! Yesterday, we learnt about the importance of goals in a man’s life. Today, we want to learn about the process of setting and re-defining your goals.",
   "key_scripture": "Habakkuk 2:2",
   "key_scripture_text": "Then the LORD answered me and said: “Write the vision And make it plain on tablets, That he may run who reads it.",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "Don’t give up! You are advancing and exceling no matter what in Jesus Name! Yesterday, we learnt about the importance of goals in a man’s life. Today, we want to learn about the process of setting and re-defining your goals."
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "The goal setting process includes;"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "1. Decide exactly what you want in a specific area of your life."
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "(Spiritual Goals, Academic Goals, Career goals, Financial Goals, Health Goals, Marriage Goals)."
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "2. Write it down. Habakkuk 2:1-2"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "A goal that is not in writing is not in writing is merely a wish or fantasy"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "3. Set a deadline for your goal. Habakkuk 2:3-4, Eccl. 3:1-2"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "A goal without a deadline has no urgency. We have Immediate goals (within 1 year), short-term goals ( 1-3 years), long-term goals (4-10 years)."
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "4. Identify the obstacles that you would have to overcome in order to"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "achieve your goals ."
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "Internal or personal obstacles: Laziness, too much leisure (TV etc.), dislike for certain subjects etc."
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "External obstacles: Wrong associations – Psalm 119:163"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "5. Make a list of everything you have to do in order to achieve your goals"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "and organize the list into a comprehensive plan. Prov. 16:1-3; Prov. 16:9"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "6. Take action on your plan immediately. An average plan vigorously"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "executed is far better than a brilliant plan on which nothing is done. Eph. 5:16, Col. 4:5"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "7. Decide to do something every day that will move you towards the"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "achievement of your goals."
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "You must be self-disciplined. You must submit yourself under rules if you want to be a ruler. There are two kinds of pain: the Pain of Discipline & the Pain of Regrets."
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "8. Depend on God’s Grace. GRACE= (G) God in the Race. When you have"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "God in the race of your life; you will eventually emerge as a winner. I Cor. 15:10"
    }
