     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "So, prayer will make you resistant to sin. In prayer we meet with the holy God where defilement gives way to divinity. In prayer we are purified, refined and sanctified. One day, Jesus took three of His disciples to the mountain to pray. In the midst of prayer, the garment of Jesus became white which is symbolic of the impartation of the Spirit of holiness - Lk.9:28-30; Is.6:1-7. The Bible says in Eccl. 9:8, ‘Let thy garments always be white and let not your head lack ointment’"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "You can’t be truly prayerful and enjoy sin. In prayer our taste for sin is destroyed and our taste for righteousness is activated."
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "Get a man to pray and you will succeed at getting him out of sin. When a person gives himself continually to prayer, the negative addictions of sin fade away. In prayer we look at God and thereafter look like God. In this second half of the year, give yourself to prayer if you desire to live holy. Have a daily prayer schedule. Watch and pray so that you will not enter into temptation. YOU CANNOT REMAIN SINFUL IF YOU ARE GENUINELY PRAYERFUL. You can be sanctified through prayer. Prayer works wonders."
