   "slug": "the-ultimate-purpose-of-study",
   "order": 59,
   "title": "The Ultimate Purpose of Study",
   "summary": "The primary purpose of study is to get information but the ultimate is to press for transformation. The whole essence of knowledge is transformation. If it is not applicable, then it is not profitable.",
   "key_scripture": "1 Timothy 4:13, 15",
   "key_scripture_text": "Till I come, give attendance to reading, to exhortation, to doctrine. Meditate upon these things; give thyself wholly to them; that thy profiting may appear to all.",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "The primary purpose of study is to get information but the ultimate is to press for transformation. The whole essence of knowledge is transformation. If it is not applicable, then it is not profitable. Information that does not culminate in transformation is wasted. Information is peripheral; it is transformation that takes you into depth. Renewal of mind must result in the transformation of life. Rom.12:2 says, “And be ye TRANSFORMED by the renewing of your minds...”"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "Don’t look for what to say but more importantly for what to show – 1 Tim.4:13,15. In your personal study, always seek for what to encounter and experience. That is the ultimate purpose of study – to experience change. If it doesn’t change you, it’s not worth it. II Cor.3:18. Therefore, whenever you are studying or gathering information analyze every information critically and see how you can apply it to specific situations or scenarios in your life. You must always draw vital conclusions from your observations. Then begin to apply all those conclusions to specific areas of your life where changes are needed. Then little by little, you will begin to see the needed changes you desire and make progress at the end of the day."
    },
    {
