  {
   "slug": "how-to-increase-your-performance",
   "order": 63,
   "title": "How to Increase Your Performance",
   "summary": "Performance in any duty or assignment is enhanced when you consider the task as a privilege. When you take any assignment for granted, you start failing at it. Every man is at his peak performance whenever it is seen as a privilege to serve.",
   "key_scripture": "1 Samuel 15:17",
   "key_scripture_text": "And Samuel said, When thou wast little in thine own sight, wast thou not made the head of the tribes of Israel, and the LORD anointed thee king over Israel?",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "Performance in any duty or assignment is enhanced when you consider the task as a privilege. When you take any assignment for granted, you start failing at it. Every man is at his peak performance whenever it is seen as a privilege to serve. God always resist the proud but gives more grace to the humble. When King Saul was little in his own sight, God anointed him and made him king over all the tribes over Israel (I Sam. 15:17). However, when he became proud and disobedient, God dethroned him and he died like a man who was never anointed. II Sam. 1:21 says, “ Ye mountains of Gilboa, let there be no dew, neither let there be rain, upon you, nor fields of offerings: for there the shield of the mighty is vilely cast away, the shield of Saul, as though he had not been anointed with oil.”"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "Don’t ever turn into a “big man” because “big men” cannot do small things and if you fail at doing small things you will never be assigned to anything bigger. You must remain small in your eyes to become qualified before God for greater task."
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "Moses assumed greatness before Pharaoh and in the land of Egypt because he resumed his task excitedly. The cup of greatness only fits well on the heads of servants. Remain a servant at heart to maintain your position on the throne. God does not anoint masters; He only anoints servants. Psalm 89:20 says, “I have found my servant David and with my holy oil have I anointed him”"
    }
   ],
