  {
   "slug": "supernatural-makeover",
   "order": 64,
   "title": "Supernatural Makeover!",
   "summary": "One of these days, you will wake up in the robes of a king in Jesus Name! My dear brother/sister, in every pain, there is a hidden gain. The challenges of life must never cause you to give up.",
   "key_scripture": "Genesis 41:37-43",
   "key_scripture_text": "Vrs. 41 “ And Pharaoh said unto Joseph, see, I have set thee over all the Lord of Egypt”.",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "One of these days, you will wake up in the robes of a king in Jesus Name! My dear brother/sister, in every pain, there is a hidden gain. The challenges of life must never cause you to give up. Whenever you are down to nothing, God is surely up to something. In world today, most Christians are looking for slight things to backslide."
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "Look at the story of Joseph critically. Many Christians of today would easily backslide if they are to experience what this young man went through. Joseph was a dreamer. In fact, all the dreams pointed to one fact “that one day he will be a ruler and a great man”. However, what he went through did not look at it all. His own brothers conspired and sold him as a slave to the Israelites and he finally landed in Egypt. In Egypt, Potiphar’s wife again put him into trouble which landed him into prison. My God, how can a “future ruler” become a “present prisoner?”"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "You must know this in life, “your prison can be a blessing in disguise”. Do you know that testimonies are borne out of tests and without a battle there is no victory? One day in Gen.41, Pharaoh dreamt and no one could explain the dream. Only one man could give the interpretation and that man was a prisoner called Joseph. After Joseph interpreted the dream, Pharaoh was too enthused with his wisdom that he made him the next in command. Today, notwithstanding what you are going through, I see God taking you out of your prison into your palace. Maybe your story is bitter but your glory will be better!!!"
    }
   ],
