   "title": "You Need Good and Proper Feeding",
   "summary": "In life, what you eat will determine whether you grow well or not. That is why when you take in a lot of protein-based foods and you begin to put on some weight people will begin to ask you the common rhetorical question, ‘What have you been eating’?",
   "key_scripture": "Jeremiah 15:16",
   "key_scripture_text": "Your words were found, and I ate them, And Your word was to me the joy and rejoicing of my heart; For I am called by Your name, O LORD God of hosts.",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "In life, what you eat will determine whether you grow well or not. That is why when you take in a lot of protein-based foods and you begin to put on some weight people will begin to ask you the common rhetorical question, ‘What have you been eating’? Such people obviously know that, you are growing well because you are feeding well!"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "Good and proper feeding is essential for your survival. In as much as our bodies need to feed well in order to grow, our spirits also need the Word of God in order to live and function well."
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "The goodness, fatness and strength of a soul are knowledge determined. That is why III John 2 says ‘Beloved, I wish above all things that you may prosper and be in health even as your soul prospers’. Your physical prosperity is therefore dependent on how well you feed your spirit."
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "If the spirit is not fed well it will be lean and famish in the end. Prov.19:2 says, ‘Also it is not good for a soul to be without knowledge...’ Life is enriched by feeding it. Feeding determines weight and weight is what measures the impact one will make."
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "Feeding is a personal responsibility we must accept. When Jeremiah located the Word, he had to take the responsibility of eating it. Jeremiah 15: 16 says ‘Your words were found, and I ate them, And Your word was to me the joy and rejoicing of my heart; For I am called by Your name, O LORD God of hosts.’"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "No one can develop your spirit for you. You have decide to daily fill yourself with the Word of God through the process of quality meditation. The Words you hide in your heart are what you will give out in times of crisis. Therefore, feed well to live well!"
    }
   ],
