     "type": "heading",
     "text": "Winning faith is an acting faith"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "Faith without action is fake. Faith is not just a fact but more importantly an act. Positive action is a clear evidence of faith at work. The Bible tells us that “Noah, being warned of God of things not seen as yet ... prepared an ark to the saving of his house...” Heb. 11:7. Also, when Abraham was called of God, by faith he obeyed and departed. Gen. 12:1-4. Furthermore, the Bible says, “Above all, taking the shield of faith, where with ye shall be able to quench all the fiery darts of the wicked.” Eph. 6:16. So, faith is a weapon of war. In order to obtain the breakthrough you desire, you have to put the weapon to good use. Until you fight, you can’t win! The kingdom of God suffereth violence, and the violent takes it by force. That force is the force of faith. When you engage in a faith battle, it is a good fight, because the end will be favourable to you. 1 Jn. 5:4."
